            </svg>
          </span>
          <span class="badge-title">Discord Text Styler & Kaomoji Generator</span>
          <span class="badge-pill-free">Free Tool</span>
        </div>

        <!-- Main Headline -->
        <h1 class="hero-headline">
          Discord <span class="gradient-text">Emoji Generator</span>
        </h1>

        <!-- Short Description -->
        <p class="hero-desc">
          Format copy-and-paste Unicode text styles, aesthetic bracket badges, and expressive Kaomojis for Discord messages, bios, nicknames, and server channel names.
        </p>

        <!-- Feature Chips Row (Zero Emojis - Clean SVG Icons) -->
        <div class="hero-features-row">
          <span class="feature-chip">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="chip-svg" aria-hidden="true">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z" />
            </svg>
            Instant Live Preview
          </span>
          <span class="feature-chip">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="chip-svg" aria-hidden="true">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M7 8h10M7 12h4m1 8l-4-4H5a2 2 0 01-2-2V6a2 2 0 012-2h14a2 2 0 012 2v8a2 2 0 01-2 2h-3l-4 4z" />
            </svg>
            Unicode Text & Kaomojis
          </span>
          <span class="feature-chip">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="chip-svg" aria-hidden="true">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m5.618-4.016A11.955 11.955 0 0112 2.944a11.955 11.955 0 01-8.618 3.04A12.02 12.02 0 003 9c0 5.591 3.824 10.29 9 11.622 5.176-1.332 9-6.03 9-11.622 0-1.042-.133-2.052-.382-3.016z" />
            </svg>
            Channel & Bio Safe
          </span>
          <span class="feature-chip">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="chip-svg" aria-hidden="true">
              <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"/>
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"/>
            </svg>
            One-Click Copy
          </span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- 2. MAIN TOOL SECTION (Container Max-Width 940px) -->
    <section class="tool-main-section" aria-label="Discord Emoji and Text Generator Interface">
      <div class="container tool-card-container">
        
        <!-- The Prominent SaaS Tool Card -->
        <div class="saas-tool-card">
          
          <!-- Card Top Bar -->
          <div class="card-header-bar">
            <div class="tool-title-group">
              <span class="tool-card-title">Discord Text & Symbol Styler</span>
              <span class="tool-card-subtitle">Format text into copyable Unicode fonts, bracket badges, and Kaomojis</span>
            </div>

            <div class="header-actions">
              <button type="button" id="btn-reset-tool" class="btn-tool-secondary" title="Reset to default text">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="btn-icon-svg" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M4 4v5h.582m15.356 2A8.001 8.001 0 004.582 9m0 0H9m11 11v-5h-.581m0 0a8.003 8.003 0 01-15.357-2m15.357 2H15" />
                </svg>
                <span>Reset</span>
              </button>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Input Field Area -->
          <div class="tool-input-section">
            <div class="input-field-group">
              <div class="field-label-row">
                <label for="input-discord-text" class="field-label">
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="label-svg" aria-hidden="true">
                    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M11 5H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v11a2 2 0 002 2h11a2 2 0 002-2v-5m-1.414-9.414a2 2 0 112.828 2.828L11.828 15H9v-2.828l8.586-8.586z" />
                  </svg>
                  <span>Text, Phrase, or Channel Title</span>
                </label>
                
                <div class="char-count-wrap">
                  <span id="char-count-text" class="char-count-badge">10 chars</span>
                  <span id="badge-limit-safety" class="limit-safety-badge safe">Channel & Bio Safe</span>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="input-wrapper">
                <input
                  type="text"
                  id="input-discord-text"
                  class="styled-text-input"
                  placeholder="Type or paste text to format..."
                  value="Gaming Hub"
                  maxlength="200"
                  aria-describedby="desc-input-text"
                />
                <button type="button" id="btn-clear-input" class="btn-clear-inside" title="Clear text" aria-label="Clear text input">
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="clear-svg" aria-hidden="true">
                    <line x1="18" y1="6" x2="6" y2="18"></line>
                    <line x1="6" y1="6" x2="18" y2="18"></line>
                  </svg>
                </button>
              </div>

              <p class="field-helper-text" id="desc-input-text">
                Discord channel names allow up to 32 characters; profile bios allow up to 190 characters.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Notice Banner: Distinguish Unicode Text vs Discord Image Emojis -->
          <div class="clarification-banner">
            <div class="banner-icon-col">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="banner-info-svg" aria-hidden="true">
                <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10" />
                <line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12" y2="12" />
                <line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12.01" y2="8" />
              </svg>
            </div>
            <div class="banner-text-col">
              <strong>Unicode Text vs. Discord Image Emojis:</strong>
              This tool formats copyable Unicode text styles, bracket badges, and Kaomojis that paste directly into Discord chat, nicknames, and bios. To upload custom image emojis (128&times;128px PNG or animated GIF) to a server, upload them directly in <em>Server Settings &gt; Emoji</em>.
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Live Mockup / Featured Output Box -->
          <div class="featured-preview-card" id="featured-preview-card">
            <div class="preview-header-bar">
              <span class="preview-badge-label">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="preview-svg-icon" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M2.036 12.322a1.012 1.012 0 010-.639C3.423 7.51 7.36 4.5 12 4.5c4.638 0 8.573 3.007 9.963 7.178.07.207.07.431 0 .639C20.577 16.49 16.64 19.5 12 19.5c-4.638 0-8.573-3.007-9.963-7.178z" />
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15 12a3 3 0 11-6 0 3 3 0 016 0z" />
                </svg>
                Live Discord Chat Preview
              </span>
              <span class="selected-style-name" id="current-selected-style-tag">Bold Sans</span>
            </div>

            <!-- Discord Mockup Message Bubble -->
            <div class="discord-message-mockup">
              <div class="mockup-avatar" aria-hidden="true">CF</div>
              <div class="mockup-content">
                <div class="mockup-meta">
                  <span class="mockup-username">Discord User</span>
                  <span class="mockup-bot-badge">Bot</span>
                  <span class="mockup-timestamp">Today at 12:43 PM</span>
                </div>
                <div class="mockup-text-bubble">
                  Check out this Discord text style: <span class="mockup-highlight" id="mockup-preview-text">𝗚𝗮𝗺𝗶𝗻𝗴 𝗛𝘂𝗯</span>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Primary Copy Action Bar -->
            <div class="preview-actions-bar">
              <div class="preview-meta-info">
                <span class="meta-label">Selected Output:</span>
                <span class="meta-value-clean" id="display-selected-raw">𝗚𝗮𝗺𝗶𝗻𝗴 𝗛𝘂𝗯</span>
              </div>

              <button type="button" id="btn-copy-featured" class="btn-copy-featured" title="Copy active style to clipboard">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" class="copy-svg" aria-hidden="true">
                  <rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"/>
                  <path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"/>
                </svg>
                <span id="copy-featured-label">Copy Selected Style</span>
              </button>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Category Filter Tabs -->
          <div class="category-tabs-row" role="tablist" aria-label="Filter style categories">
            <button type="button" class="category-tab active" data-category="all" role="tab" aria-selected="true">
              All Styles (<span id="count-all">37</span>)
            </button>
            <button type="button" class="category-tab" data-category="unicode" role="tab" aria-selected="false">
              Unicode Fonts (<span id="count-unicode">11</span>)
            </button>
            <button type="button" class="category-tab" data-category="badges" role="tab" aria-selected="false">
              Badges & Brackets (<span id="count-badges">10</span>)
            </button>
            <button type="button" class="category-tab" data-category="kaomoji" role="tab" aria-selected="false">
              Kaomoji Combos (<span id="count-kaomoji">10</span>)
            </button>
            <button type="button" class="category-tab" data-category="dividers" role="tab" aria-selected="false">
              Dividers & Frames (<span id="count-dividers">6</span>)
            </button>
          </div>

          <!-- Empty State (Hidden when input has content) -->
          <div class="empty-state-card hidden" id="empty-state-card">
            <div class="empty-icon-wrap">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" class="empty-svg" aria-hidden="true">
                <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M16.862 4.487l1.687-1.688a1.875 1.875 0 112.652 2.652L6.832 19.82a4.5 4.5 0 01-1.897 1.13l-2.685.8.8-2.685a4.5 4.5 0 011.13-1.897L16.863 4.487zm0 0L19.5 7.125" />
              </svg>
            </div>
            <h3 class="empty-title">Enter Text to Generate Styles</h3>
            <p class="empty-desc">
              Type or paste words in the input box above to instantly generate Discord text styles, aesthetic bracket badges, and Kaomojis.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- Results Grid Container -->
          <div class="results-grid-wrapper" id="results-grid-wrapper">
            <div class="styles-output-grid" id="styles-output-grid">
              <!-- Dynamically populated style cards -->
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 3. COMPREHENSIVE EDITORIAL & SEO CONTENT (Max-Width 940px) -->
    <section class="tool-content-section" aria-label="Discord Text Styling and Custom Emoji Guide">
      <div class="container content-inner-container">
        
        <!-- Editorial Guide Card -->
        <div class="content-card">
          
          <div class="editorial-block">
            <span class="content-pill">Discord Formatting & Custom Emoji Guide</span>
            
            <h2>What Is a Discord Emoji Generator and How Does It Work?</h2>
            <p>
              A <strong>Discord Emoji Generator</strong> is a specialized text formatting and aesthetic styling tool built for community administrators, streamers, content creators, and casual gamers who want to make their text chat and profile presentation stand out. While standard Discord emojis provide graphical stickers and reactions, text-based styling utilizes Unicode mathematical alphanumeric symbols, Japanese emoticons (Kaomojis), decorative bracket frames, and typographical glyphs. These stylized characters transform standard plain keyboard input into visually distinct headers, channel badges, custom status tags, and expressive chat messages.
            </p>
            <p>
              Instead of hunting through Unicode tables, manually copying individual symbols, or guessing whether a character will render properly inside Discord desktop and mobile applications, a <strong>Discord text generator</strong> instantly transforms your input across dozens of curated aesthetic styles. Whether you are organizing Discord channel hierarchies with clean bracket badges, adding personality to your user profile card, or designing celebratory chat announcements, this <strong>Discord symbols generator</strong> provides immediate, real-time conversion with one-click clipboard copying.
            </p>

            <h2>Unicode Text Styles vs. Custom Discord Emoji Images: Key Differences</h2>
            <p>
              To understand how to make the most of this tool, it is essential to distinguish between two distinct features in the Discord ecosystem: copyable Unicode text styles and custom server image emojis.
            </p>
            <ul class="styled-list">
              <li><strong>Unicode Text Styles and Symbols:</strong> Unicode characters are universal typographical glyphs built directly into modern operating systems and web standards. When you format a phrase into bold sans (such as 𝗚𝗮𝗺𝗶𝗻𝗴 𝗛𝘂𝗯), bracketed badges (such as 『 GAMING HUB 』), or a Kaomoji text face (such as (•_•)), you are producing standard text strings. These characters can be pasted into Discord text channels, direct messages, user bios, server nicknames, and voice channel titles. They do not require server administration privileges, and they are universally visible to all Discord users without requiring a paid Discord Nitro subscription.</li>
              <li><strong>Custom Discord Emoji Images:</strong> In contrast, <strong>custom Discord emojis</strong> are discrete 128&times;128 pixel graphic images (PNG, JPG, WEBP, or animated GIF files) that server managers upload directly into Discord's server settings. Custom image emojis occupy dedicated server emote slots (50 slots on standard servers, up to 250 on Tier 3 boosted servers). They are triggered using colon syntax (such as <code>:custom_emote:</code>) and can only be used in external servers by users with active Discord Nitro memberships. Our tool specializes in formatting universal Unicode text, badges, and Kaomojis that copy and paste anywhere in Discord instantly.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>How to Generate, Preview, and Copy Styled Discord Text</h2>
            <p>
              Generating <strong>Discord text styles</strong> and aesthetic Kaomojis with this tool is straightforward and requires zero technical setup:
            </p>
            <ol class="styled-ordered-list">
              <li><strong>Enter Your Text:</strong> Enter your text, keyword, or phrase into the input field at the top of the calculator.</li>
              <li><strong>Filter by Style Category:</strong> Browse all variations or filter by specific styling categories such as Unicode Fonts, Badges &amp; Brackets, Kaomoji Combos, or Dividers.</li>
              <li><strong>Inspect the Live Chat Preview:</strong> Review the live Discord message preview bubble to see exactly how your chosen text format renders within a realistic chat bubble.</li>
              <li><strong>Copy with One Click:</strong> Click the Copy button on your preferred style card or the main featured preview bar to save the formatted text directly to your clipboard.</li>
              <li><strong>Paste into Discord:</strong> Open Discord and paste the styled text into your target chat channel, user bio, server nickname, or channel name.</li>
            </ol>

            <h2>Where You Can Use Generated Text, Badges, and Symbols in Discord</h2>
            <p>
              Because Discord is built on flexible text fields, you can <strong>copy and paste Discord symbols</strong> and styled fonts across multiple areas of your server and user profile:
            </p>
            <ul class="styled-list">
              <li><strong>Server Channel Names and Category Headers:</strong> Community managers use bracket badges (such as 『announcements』, 【rules】, or ✦-welcome) to create clean visual hierarchy in their server sidebar. If you are launching a new server, pair these styles with our <a href="/tools/discord-server-name-generator">Discord Server Name Generator</a>.</li>
              <li><strong>User Profile "About Me" Bios:</strong> Discord user bios have a 190-character budget. Dense Unicode badges and Kaomojis help you express your identity, gaming handles, and social links within character limits. Explore our <a href="/tools/discord-bio-generator">Discord Bio Generator</a> for full profile layouts.</li>
              <li><strong>Server Nicknames:</strong> Customize your display name within specific gaming guilds by pairing small caps or bold font styles with your gamertag. For fresh handle ideas, try our <a href="/tools/discord-username-generator">Discord Username Generator</a> or <a href="/tools/twitch-username-generator">Twitch Username Generator</a>.</li>
              <li><strong>Chat Announcements and Event Highlights:</strong> Stand out in busy channels by framing important notices with decorative symbol dividers, quote lines, or celebratory Kaomojis. You can also format text for other platforms using our <a href="/tools/instagram-font-generator">Instagram Font Generator</a>.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Cross-Platform Font Rendering and Screen Reader Accessibility</h2>
            <p>
              When utilizing styled Unicode text online, creators should understand font rendering mechanics across modern hardware. Unicode mathematical alphanumerics (such as bold, script, and monospace characters) were originally cataloged in the Unicode standard for scientific and mathematical notation. While modern operating systems like Windows 10/11, macOS, iOS, Android, and modern Linux distributions natively render these glyphs, older devices or customized Android skins may occasionally display missing glyphs as empty rectangles or question marks (commonly known as "tofu" boxes).
            </p>
            <p>
              Accessibility is another vital factor to consider when designing Discord text. Screen reading software utilized by visually impaired community members interprets standard text effortlessly. However, when a screen reader encounters mathematical alphanumeric Unicode characters, it announces each glyph individually (for example, reading 𝗚 as "mathematical sans-serif bold capital G"). To maintain an inclusive and accessible server community, reserve heavy Unicode styling for short accent words, channel badges, and headings, rather than formatting entire multi-sentence message bodies.
            </p>

            <h2>Troubleshooting Common Copying, Pasting, and Display Issues</h2>
            <p>
              If you encounter issues when copying, pasting, or displaying styled Discord text, review these practical troubleshooting tips:
            </p>
            <ul class="styled-list">
              <li><strong>Missing Glyph or Tofu Boxes:</strong> If a recipient sees a hollow square or question mark box instead of your formatted text, their device operating system is likely running an outdated font library. Sticking with standard brackets and classic Kaomojis ensures 100% universal rendering across all hardware.</li>
              <li><strong>Character Limit Exceeded:</strong> Discord enforces specific character boundaries: 32 characters for server channel names, 190 characters for user bios, and 2,000 characters for standard chat messages (4,000 for Nitro). Certain complex Unicode glyphs and combining diacritics occupy multiple bytes in UTF-16 encoding, which can consume character allowances faster than plain Latin characters. Always verify character counts with our live counter.</li>
              <li><strong>Channel Name Lowercase Formatting:</strong> Discord automatically converts standard text channel names to lowercase and replaces spaces with hyphens. Using Unicode symbols or bracket frames allows server creators to bypass monotonous plain text and craft aesthetically branded channel headers.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Official Discord Custom Emoji Upload Specifications at a Glance</h2>
            <p>
              If you also manage a Discord server and wish to upload graphic image emojis alongside your styled text, adhere to Discord's official specifications:
            </p>
            <ul class="styled-list">
              <li><strong>File Dimensions:</strong> Exactly 128&times;128 pixels is the recommended standard resolution for crisp display across mobile and desktop clients. Discord automatically scales images down to 32&times;32 pixels in chat messages.</li>
              <li><strong>File Formats:</strong> Square PNG images with transparent backgrounds are ideal for static emotes. Animated emotes require GIF format.</li>
              <li><strong>File Size Ceiling:</strong> Each uploaded image or GIF must not exceed 256 KB.</li>
              <li><strong>Slot Capacity:</strong> Non-boosted standard servers include 50 custom static emoji slots and 50 custom animated emoji slots. Boosting a server to Level 1 unlocks 100 total slots, Level 2 unlocks 150 slots, and Level 3 unlocks 250 slots.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
              By combining custom image uploads with styled Unicode text, Kaomojis, and decorative brackets from our <strong>Discord emoji maker</strong>, server owners can establish a memorable visual brand across every channel.
            </p>
          </div>

          <!-- High-Value Search FAQs Section -->
